# The dust in the Barrow of Kings' hall (TSC_Spot_DustLine, Perception):
# the first niche in the procession, and the first hint that something at
# the deep end of the floor is not as sealed as it looks.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_DustLine

== start ==
Dust settles evenly in still air, and this has not. Under the lamp there is a faint grain to it, every mote lain down along the same line, combed by air that has been moving over this floor very slowly for a very long time.

* [Follow the grain.] -> follow

== follow ==
The grain runs the length of the hall, all of it pointing one direction: toward the deep end of the floor, and whatever the deep end holds.

Sealed rooms do not breathe. Something down there is not sealed as well as it looks, and it has been drawing slow breath since before the kingdom fell.

* [Keep walking, and keep count of your own breathing.] -> end
